    "summary": "High‑energy set with soaring Dark Star → Brokedown Palace and tight Playin'",
    "blurb": "The concert bursts open with a smoking Dark Star → Brokedown Palace and a fiery Playing In The Band that drive the first half. Jerry delivers some of his best vocals on Bird Song and Morning Dew while the rhythm section keeps the momentum high throughout. Recording sources vary, but the excellent matrix mix captures the performance with crystal‑clear detail.",
    "review": "September 16, 1972 at Boston Music Hall finds the Dead firing on all cylinders. The first set rolls through classics like Bertha and Big River before launching into a scorching Bird Song that showcases Garcia’s soaring vocals, then ramps up to an incandescent Playing In The Band. The second set is anchored by a legendary Dark Star that seamlessly segues into a luminous Brokedown Palace; the improvisation is both growling and space‑filled, with Keith’s piano adding texture and Ned Lagin’s Wurlitzer giving the jam an extra edge. A tight rhythm section—Bill chugging like a machine and Phil pushing the low end despite occasional thinness—keeps the groove solid while Bob weaves his rhythm guitar around the vortex. The show closes on a joyous One More Saturday Night, leaving the audience buzzing. Among the available sources, the matrix recording (gd1972-09-16.matrix.sb20.chappell.77442.flac16) delivers an in‑room feel and superb clarity that lets every nuance of this high‑energy performance shine.",
